WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.513
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:09.222
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:17.388
Unit thirteen: Part 5: Prepositions and Conjunctions. Today you will choose prepositions, conjunctions and linking words correctly.

4
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:20.410
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.925
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:26.854
Preposition.

7
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.616
Preposition means a word like in, on or at.

8
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:32.659
At is a preposition.

9
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.065
Your turn. Say: Preposition.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.889
Preposition.

11
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:41.663
Conjunction.

12
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.381
Conjunction means a word that joins ideas.

13
00:00:45.983 --> 00:00:47.507
Although is a conjunction.

14
00:00:48.117 --> 00:00:50.537
Your turn. Say: Conjunction.

15
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.482
Conjunction.

16
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:56.160
Although.

17
00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.289
Although means in spite of the fact that.

18
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:01.442
Although it rained, we worked.

19
00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.180
Your turn. Say: Although.

20
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.069
Although.

21
00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:09.725
Because of.

22
00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:12.763
Because of means as a result of.

23
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.535
Because of the delay, we left late.

24
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.733
Your turn. Say: Because of.

25
00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:22.521
Because of.

26
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.226
Despite.

27
00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.949
Despite means in spite of.

28
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.468
Despite the cost, we bought it.

29
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.480
Your turn. Say: Despite.

30
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:36.230
Despite.

31
00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:38.031
Unless.

32
00:01:39.017 --> 00:01:40.703
Unless means if not.

33
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:43.339
Unless you sign, we cannot start.

34
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.382
Your turn. Say: Unless.

35
00:01:49.233 --> 00:01:50.281
Unless.

36
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:51.820
By.

37
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:54.352
By means not later than.

38
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.450
Send it by Friday.

39
00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.331
Your turn. Say: By.

40
00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.075
By.

41
00:02:03.817 --> 00:02:05.004
Until.

42
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:07.970
Until means up to a certain time.

43
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:09.805
Wait until noon.

44
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:12.814
Your turn. Say: Until.

45
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:16.668
Until.

46
00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:21.617
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.483 --> 00:02:25.876
Visal, why do students confuse although and despite?

48
00:02:26.983 --> 00:02:40.096
Although is a conjunction, so a clause follows it: although it was expensive. Despite is a preposition, so a noun or an -ing form follows: despite the price.

49
00:02:41.183 --> 00:02:42.997
What about by and until?

50
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:53.284
By means no later than, for example, submit it by Friday. Until means up to a time and shows continuation, such as I will wait until noon.

51
00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:55.953
How do I choose quickly?

52
00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:05.647
Look at what comes after the gap: a clause or a noun. Then check the meaning: contrast, reason, time or condition.

53
00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.521
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:13.078
Grammar focus: Strategy: what follows the gap?.

55
00:03:13.378 --> 00:03:14.692
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:18.579
Although the price was high, we signed the contract.

57
00:03:19.483 --> 00:03:22.156
Despite the high price, we signed the contract.

58
00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:29.059
Check whether a clause or a noun follows the gap, then choose a conjunction or a preposition with the right meaning.

59
00:03:29.817 --> 00:03:33.897
Be careful! Don't say: I use despite before a clause.

60
00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:38.692
Say: I use although before a clause.

61
00:03:38.992 --> 00:03:40.469
Despite + noun.

62
00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.977
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.174
Choosing the Right Word.

64
00:03:46.474 --> 00:03:50.053
The sentence says: ___ the high price, the team bought the machine.

65
00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:54.378
A noun phrase follows the gap, so a preposition is needed.

66
00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.318
The options are although, despite, because and unless.

67
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:02.088
The meaning is contrast, so Despite fits.

68
00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.448
Rotha chooses Despite and moves on.

69
00:04:06.533 --> 00:04:10.674
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.087
A clause follows blank.

71
00:04:13.387 --> 00:04:17.156
A, by. B, although. C, despite.

72
00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.711
The answer is B: although.

73
00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.408
'By Friday' means blank.

74
00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:30.639
A, until Friday ends. B, after Friday. C, no later than Friday.

75
00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.768
The answer is C: no later than Friday.

76
00:04:37.917 --> 00:04:39.405
'Unless' means blank.

77
00:04:39.705 --> 00:04:43.057
A, if not. B, because. C, although.

78
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.240
The answer is A: if not.

79
00:04:49.383 --> 00:04:52.242
Which fits: blank the high price, we bought it?

80
00:04:52.542 --> 00:04:56.300
A, Unless. B, Despite. C, Although.

81
00:04:59.833 --> 00:05:01.937
The answer is B: Despite.

82
00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:04.677
What follows 'despite'?

83
00:05:04.977 --> 00:05:09.617
A, a full clause only. B, nothing. C, a noun or -ing form.

84
00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.898
The answer is C: a noun or -ing form.

85
00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:20.066
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.917 --> 00:05:23.311
How do you choose between although and despite?

87
00:05:32.117 --> 00:05:33.489
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:33.789 --> 00:05:48.286
I look at what follows the gap. If a clause follows, I use although, and if a noun or an -ing form follows, I use despite. Both show contrast, so the meaning is the same but the grammar is different.

89
00:05:48.586 --> 00:05:50.377
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:56.200
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: what follows the gap?.

91
00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:01.764
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:02.064 --> 00:06:04.775
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:05.075 --> 00:06:08.482
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

